$ efsd --help
efsd - Run an EFS storage node

Usage:
  efsd --node-id ID --addr ADDRESS --port PORT --storage PATH [options]

Options:
  --node-id ID          Node identifier
  --addr ADDRESS        Listen address
  --port PORT           Listen port
  --storage PATH        Storage roots; repeat or separate with commas
  --quota SIZE          Storage quota; accepts K, M, G and T suffixes
  --direct-io           Use O_DIRECT for fragment I/O
  --no-direct-io        Use buffered fragment I/O (default)
  --writers N           Shared writer threads; 0 runs writes inline
  --join HOST:PORT      Join an existing cluster
  --meta-storage PATH   Raft/KV root (default: first storage root)
  --no-persist          Disable cluster configuration persistence
  --perf                Record a CPU profile
  --strace              Record system calls
  -h, --help            Show this help
  --version             Show the program version

Examples:
  efsd --node-id 1 --addr 127.0.0.1 --port 17432 --storage /data1/efs/n1

Notes:
  Metadata root changes do not move existing mdraft data.
  Storage roots use least-queue write placement across paths.

