$ efs-fuse --help
efs-fuse - Mount an EFS export

Usage:
  efs-fuse NODE:PORT [NODE:PORT ...] EXPORT MOUNTPOINT [options]

Options:
  -o OPTIONS            FUSE mount options
  --perf                Record a CPU profile
  --strace              Record system calls
  --stop MOUNTPOINT     Drain and stop a mounted client
  --resume MOUNTPOINT   Resume a drained client
  -h, --help            Show this help
  --version             Show the program version

Examples:
  efs-fuse 127.0.0.1:17432 fs /data1/efs/mnt
  EFS_COMMANDS=1 efs-fuse 127.0.0.1:17432 fs /data1/efs/mnt

Notes:
  One node address is enough; the client discovers the other nodes.
  EFS_COMMANDS=1 enables directory-local .efs commands on this mount.
  Those commands require Python 3 on the machine executing them.
  Use --stop MOUNTPOINT --force-discard only to discard pending writes.
  Use --help-fuse for the underlying FUSE option reference.

