$ efs-bench --help
efs-bench - Measure EFS network, storage and metadata performance

Usage:
  efs-bench [NODE:PORT] MODE [options]

Commands:
  --time SEC            Network ceiling; servers ACK and discard data
  --size SIZE           Write real protected data (K/M/G/T suffixes)
  --store --time SEC    Timed disk writes
  --read --time SEC     Timed disk reads
  --meta                Metadata RPC workload
  --bench io            Raw storage I/O (no cluster)
  --bench io-blake3     Raw I/O with timed hashing
  --bench blake3        CPU hashing (no storage or cluster)
  --bench data          Local data engine (no cluster)
  --bench meta          Local metadata engine (no cluster)
  --bench principles    Independent EFS-shaped storage experiments

Options:
  --window N            Read window in chunks
  --export NAME         Metadata export
  --files N             Metadata file count
  --dirs N              Metadata directory count
  --workers N           Metadata workers
  --phases CSV          Metadata phases
  --keep                Keep metadata fixture
  --id N                Chunk-index base for parallel writers
  --perf                Record a CPU profile
  -h, --help            Show this help
  --version             Show the program version

Examples:
  efs-bench 127.0.0.1:17432 --store --time 10
  efs-bench --bench data --help
  efs-bench --bench principles --help

Notes:
  Run efs-bench --bench MODE --help for local mode options.
  Cluster modes discover all servers from one node address.

