$ efs-bench --bench data --help
efs-bench - Measure local EFS storage engines

Usage:
  efs-bench --bench data|meta --storage EMPTY_ROOT [options]

Options:
  --storage PATH        Data scratch roots; repeat or comma-separate
  --meta-storage PATH   Metadata scratch root
  --time SEC            Duration (default: 10)
  --writers N           Writer threads
  --qd N                Queue depth
  --window N            Bounded fragments per slot
  --rw TYPE             read, write or both
  --write-mode TYPE     create or overwrite
  --direct-io           Use O_DIRECT
  --no-direct-io        Use buffered I/O
  --sync                Use O_SYNC for engine writes
  --full-paths          Skip the path-prefix ladder
  --writer-stats        Measure writer waits
  --skip-ceiling        Skip the separate raw/fio ceiling probe
  --perf                Record a CPU profile
  -h, --help            Show this help
  --version             Show the program version

Examples:
  efs-bench --bench data --storage /data1/bench --time 10
  efs-bench --bench meta --meta-storage /data1/meta-bench --time 10

Notes:
  Local engines: no cluster or sockets. Scratch roots must be empty.
  Read/overwrite requires --window; create requires no window.
  Bounded windows are populated before timing.
  Percentile buckets have less than 0.782% width; maximum is exact.

