$ efs-bench --bench io --help
efs-bench - Measure raw storage I/O

Usage:
  efs-bench --bench io|io-blake3 --storage EMPTY_ROOT [options]

Options:
  --storage PATH        Scratch root; may repeat
  --rw read|write       I/O direction
  --io-size SIZE        I/O size (default: 64K)
  --qd N                Parallel workers (default: 16)
  --window N            Blocks per worker (default: 64)
  --time SEC            Duration (default: 3)
  --direct-io           Use O_DIRECT
  --no-direct-io        Use buffered I/O
  --sync                Include fdatasync after each write
  --preallocate         Allocate and populate the window before timing
  -h, --help            Show this help
  --version             Show the program version

Examples:
  efs-bench --bench io --storage /data1/bench --rw write --direct-io

Notes:
  No EFS store or network is used. Scratch roots must be empty.
  io-blake3 hashes writes and verifies reads inside the timed loop.
  Read files are populated first; written blocks are checked afterward.
  Buffered writes without --sync measure page-cache acceptance.
  Direct I/O sizes must be aligned to 4 KiB.

