$ efs-bench --bench principles --help
efs-bench - Test EFS-shaped storage principles

Usage:
  efs-bench --bench principles --storage EMPTY_ROOT [options]

Options:
  --storage PATH        Empty scratch root; may repeat
  --layout TYPE         files or container
  --rw TYPE             read, write or delete
  --policy TYPE         populated, allocating, overwrite, unlink, punch or release
  --persist TYPE        none, each or batch
  --objects N           Object count
  --payload-size SIZE   Payload bytes
  --qd N                Parallel workers
  --batch-size N        Objects per durability batch
  --direct-io           Use O_DIRECT
  --no-direct-io        Use buffered I/O
  -h, --help            Show this help
  --version             Show the program version

Examples:
  efs-bench --bench principles --storage /data1/bench --layout files

Notes:
  Independent principle driver; no production engine or cluster.
  Fixtures make one finite pass, rather than --time loops.
  Payloads have a 32-byte checksum tail; direct records use a 4 KiB tail.
  each/batch includes required file and directory fsync in wall time.

